From 35eb3e952b4e5ead088f4769aaeb976b04ab7ee7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shogo <agent@shogo.ai>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:43:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ai): verified model chain, real tool calling, real
 memory context

The assistant could not act, could not read any of Sri's data, and could swap
models mid-conversation without saying so. All three fixed and verified.

Models
- Chain is now built from live probe results, not assumption. scripts/probe-models.mjs
  checks every id against the gateway.
- Removed gpt-5-nano: it returns HTTP 200 with an EMPTY body, so it counted as
  healthy while answering nothing, and cost ~10s before handing the turn off.
- Added Hoshi 2.0, addressed by UUID (the gateway rejects its display name). The
  UUID is re-resolved on every boot so it cannot rot.
- refreshModelCatalog() probes all models in parallel 2.5s after boot, cached 10
  minutes, also callable via POST /api/ai/models/refresh. A model is healthy only
  because a probe just watched it answer.
- PREMIUM_MODELS (Sonnet 5, GPT-5.5, GPT-6 Astra, ...) 403 on this plan. Listed
  for display only; never used to answer.

Never fall back silently
- sessionModel pins the model that last answered, per session.
- Transient errors retry the SAME model once; permanent errors (403/401/404,
  'not supported') move on immediately.
- An empty response is a failure, never a success.
- If the chain does move, switchedFrom is returned and the UI says so. Verified
  for Pro-only ids and unknown ids, which previously reported nothing.
- toolsEnabled=false is honoured.

Real context and real actions
- buildUserContext() injects memories, notes, open reminders, habits, metrics and
  recent activity from SQLite into the system prompt. Previously the model was
  told about Sri by a hard-coded paragraph and correctly reported that it had no
  access to his notes.
- buildJarvisTools() adds 13 real tools (save/search memory, create/list notes,
  create/list reminders, log/list habits, log metric, read inbox, weather, news,
  recent activity). All 6 chain models verified to support tool calling.
- Tools record what they did; the chat route returns toolsUsed and the UI renders
  an 'Actions taken' block, so 'done' is always backed by a recorded action.
- System prompt rewritten: it names the real tools and states what is impossible
  (send email, calendar, acting unprompted) instead of claiming it can do anything.

Verification: bun x tsc --noEmit clean in app code; scripts/verify-capabilities.mjs
and scripts/verify-fallback.mjs pass end-to-end against the live API and delete
their own data in the same run.
